# llm.rules

See core.rules for documentation standards.

## Purpose
Defines how AutoPlex uses Qwen 3 23B A22B via OpenRouter.ai for all LLM-driven tasks such as query translation, recommendations, and search.

## Model Info
- qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b:free (OpenRouter.ai)
- Integrated with Langchain
- Used in agents and chains

## Responsibilities
- Natural-language to SQL translation
- Recommendation generation
- Query intent parsing
- User-specific chat history memory
- Triggering requests via tool use
- (optional) Text embeddings for vector store (if supported)

## Prompting
- Provide full system context: media types, DB schema, tools
- Prime with few-shot examples
- Request structured JSON for tool actions or SQL

## Tools
- `query_db(query: str)`
- `recommend(user_id: str)`
- `request_media(title, media_type, year)`

## Output Policy
- Sanitize SQL
- Validate all outputs with schema
- Never hallucinate media entries

## Vector/RAG Support
- Use summary + cast + genres for embeddings
- Embed all media on ingest
- RAG layer adds context before LLM prompt
- Use cosine similarity for retrieval
- Optional fallback to full-text SQL

## Safety
- No shell, no file system access
- Never guess metadata
- Prompt injection guarded by sanitizer

## Logging
- Log prompt, model, output, latency, token usage
- Store failed outputs for debugging
